WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.000
Today, Europe as a political entity has a chance

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.239
it never had in its long and turbulent history.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.280
The chance to organise itself

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.800
in a truly just and peaceful way

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.039
on the principle of equality and cooperation of all.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.000
To reflect on Europeanism is to ask

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.039
what the ideals or principles are

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:33.039
that the notion of Europe evokes

00:00:33.039 --> 00:00:35.239
or is characteristic of Europe.

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:37.639
I have the feeling that in my youth,

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:40.239
I would have felt a bit ridiculous

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.600
if I said or wrote that I was European,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.079
that I felt and thought like a European.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:50.079
And that's probably how it is for most Europeans.

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:53.079
They are quintessentially European,

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:55.039
but they don't realise it.

00:00:56.119 --> 00:00:57.519
It was no accident that,

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:01.119
shortly after the communist dictatorship was established,

00:01:01.119 --> 00:01:08.639
it began to violently destroy the fibres of civil society

00:01:08.639 --> 00:01:10.759
and essentially eliminate it.

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:14.839
What was left of authentic civil society lived

00:01:14.839 --> 00:01:19.479
and evolved as direct or indirect resistance.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:24.000
The task of helping new democracies in this respect

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.839
should be a natural part of our larger task:

00:01:27.839 --> 00:01:31.280
continuously deepening and strengthening

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.839
civil society on a pan-European scale.

00:01:35.839 --> 00:01:39.280
Respect for human life and human freedom

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.519
as well as consideration for pan-European security

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:45.479
may require intervention beyond the borders

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:49.839
of the European Union as a last resort.

00:01:49.839 --> 00:01:52.000
Both in Kosovo and Serbia

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
and in Bosnia and Herzegovina,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.600
in other parts of the former Yugoslavia too,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.239
tens of thousands of human lives and immeasurable material value

00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:03.639
could have been spared

00:02:03.639 --> 00:02:07.039
had the international community been able to intervene earlier

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:13.039
in an appropriate manner at the beginning of the conflicts.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.879
Evil must be nipped in the bud

00:02:20.879 --> 00:02:24.680
and it is not enough if it is confronted only by governments.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:28.479
The attitude of governments must grow out of citizens' attitudes.

00:02:33.159 --> 00:02:36.720
We all know that the enlargement of the European Union

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.600
is conceivable only when accompanied

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.400
with a continuous and no less courageous reform of its institutions.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.239
I would be happy if the country from which I come

00:02:47.239 --> 00:02:53.959
could participate as a full partner in all of this.

00:02:53.959 --> 00:02:56.839
Thank you for your attention.

